course: dictionary
lesson: 250
title: The alphabet and its order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The alphabet is the set of letters used to write a language, always put in the same fixed order. In English that order runs from A to Z. When you see «in alphabetical order», the words are arranged by their first letters, following that set order.
explain: The word also has a second meaning. Kieran's sentence, «who can burp the alphabet furthest», shows the alphabet as a set of letters said in order, one after another. Context tells you which meaning is in use: a list of letters, or a set of letters for writing.
explain: Different languages have different alphabets. «Chinese writing never became an alphabet» because it uses thousands of characters, while English uses only 26 letters. Greek, Cyrillic and Arabic are other alphabets, each with its own letters.
fact: The alphabet is the set of letters used to write a language, put in a fixed order.
fact: The English alphabet has 26 letters, from A to Z.
fact: Five English vowels are a, e, i, o and u; the other 21 letters are consonants, and y can act as both.
fact: «Alphabetical order» is used in dictionaries, registers and indexes to find words and names quickly.
fact: «About 3,800 years ago», people in Egypt and Sinai began using picture-signs for the first sound of each name: this was the first alphabet.
exercise: «The Phoenicians spread a 22-letter alphabet about 3,000 years ago.» How many letters did that alphabet have? | 18 | *22 | 5 | 26
exercise: What order are the words in a dictionary put in? | Length order | Colour order | *Alphabetical order | Random order
exercise: How many vowels does the English alphabet have, not counting y? | 3 | *5 | 26 | 21
test: «Chinese writing never became an alphabet: it uses thousands of characters.» What makes an alphabet different from Chinese writing? | It uses thousands of characters | *It uses a small set of letters | It has no order at all | It is written only on newspapers
test: What do we mean when we say the alphabet of a subject? | Its most difficult part | *Its basics, the first things you need to learn | A long book about it | A list of its famous people
exam: Which of these is a pangram, a sentence that uses every letter of the alphabet at least once? | A dictionary entry | A register of names | *«The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» | A list of numbers
